--[[
The Saule Linux installer: what a computer started from the USB stick
shows. It asks which disk, says what is on it before anything is erased,
installs, and restarts.

  saule run .     on a desktop, to see it; set SAULE_INSTALL=dev/fake-install
                  and it installs nothing, on disks that aren't there

On the stick init starts it as the session, as root (`saule.installer=1`
on the kernel command line: see ../init/src/cmdline.rs). The writing is
done by `saule-install` (../install), which this runs and watches.

    model   the disks, the installation under way, and `saule-install`
    theme   colours and sizes
    views   the pieces a page is made of
    pages   one view per step

How it ends tells init what to do next: see `Installation.exitCode`.
]]

from uikit import App
from InstallerApp import InstallerApp

class Main
  static fn main()
    local app = InstallerApp()
    app.run()

    if app.installation.exitCode != 0 then
      Os.exit(app.installation.exitCode)
    end
  end
end
